cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PIR, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "PIR: Physics Intermediate Representation"
abstract: >-
  A torch-free symbolic regression engine for recovering closed-form physical
  laws from tabular data, with exact rational and exponential fallback gates,
  a noise-tolerant power-law gate, a deterministic separability stage for
  products of sub-laws (including sign-changing, root and sin/cos factors),
  a noise-tolerant stage with validated acceptance for noisy data, and an
  optional safeguard that falls back to a linear
  model or the mean when no law fits.
